---
import AnalyticsOptOut from "@components/AnalyticsOptOut.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy – How I handle your data"
  description="How I handle your data when visiting the site."
>
  <PageHeader title="Privacy – How I handle your data" />

  <div class="prose">
    <p>2026-09-04</p>
    <p>
      I run this site personally, not as a company. If you email me, your
      message and address stay in my email archive. Nothing goes on a mailing
      list, nothing is shared, and I'll delete a message on request.
    </p>
    <p>Edvin Lindén, hello@edvinlinden.se</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      I use TelemetryDeck to see how many people visit this site and which pages
      they read. When you load a page, this is sent:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The page you visited, and the page that referred you</li>
      <li>Your browser, operating system, screen size and language</li>
      <li>Your country, derived from your IP address</li>
      <li>The time of the visit</li>
      <li>A daily-changing, anonymized visitor ID</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Clicking a link to the App Store sends one more event: where on the page
      that link was, and which page you clicked it from. Nothing else you do on
      the site is recorded.
    </p>
    <p>
      No cookies. Nothing is written to or read from your device unless you opt
      out below, and that opt-out setting is the only thing this site ever looks
      for there.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, legitimate interests in knowing whether
      what I publish here gets read. The data is minimal, no lasting identifier
      is created, nothing is stored on your device, and none of it is used to
      profile you or shared with anyone.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics provider: TelemetryDeck GmbH, Augsburg, Germany. Data is hosted
      in the EU and not transferred outside it. Their policy:
      telemetrydeck.com/privacy
    </p>
    <p>Retention: 24 months</p>

    <h2>Opting out</h2>
    <p>
      Use the switch below and analytics stops for you on this site,
      immediately and on this page. It saves one opt-out setting in your
      browser, so it covers this browser on this device, and the same switch
      turns it back on. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal,
      analytics is skipped automatically and there is nothing for the switch to
      do. Everything on the site works the same either way.
    </p>
    <AnalyticsOptOut />

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages, operated by GitHub, Inc. (United States). GitHub receives
      your IP address to deliver the page and records it in its own logs for
      security and abuse prevention. I have no access to those logs and no
      control over how long GitHub keeps them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, legitimate interests in running the
      site securely.
    </p>
    <p>
      GitHub is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and also
      relies on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses. Details:
      docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask me to access, correct, delete or restrict your personal data,
      object to how I use it, or receive a copy. Email me.
    </p>
    <p>
      The analytics data holds nothing that identifies you and no lasting
      identifier, so I can't find your records in it. Article 11 GDPR doesn't
      require me to start collecting more about you to make that possible, and I
      won't. What I can do is stop collecting from you, which is what the
      switch above does.
    </p>
    <p>
      You have the right to lodge a complaint with the Swedish data protection
      authority, Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten (IMY), or with the supervisory
      authority where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated. Changes are published on this page with a new
      effective date.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
